# The template is a control file that is read without an error, apart from
# the file of the positions, which it does not come with.
#
# RUN: mdir template md > %t.toml
# RUN: not mdir run %t.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: mdir template md | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TEMPLATE

# CHECK: cannot read '{{.*}}system.pdb'

# TEMPLATE: [input]
# TEMPLATE: [energy]
# TEMPLATE: {{\[\[}}energy.pair]]
# TEMPLATE: [dynamics]
# TEMPLATE: [execution]

# The template of a run from an Amber topology reads without an error with
# the files of examples/ala3.
#
# RUN: mdir template amber | sed -e 's|"system.prmtop"|"%S/../../examples/ala3/ala3.prmtop"|' \
# RUN:     -e 's|"system.inpcrd"|"%S/../../examples/ala3/ala3.inpcrd"|' > %t.amber.toml
# RUN: mdir check %t.amber.toml | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=AMBER
# AMBER: particles: {{ *}}4905
# AMBER: degrees of freedom: 7387
